<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  Mortalive — sitemap.xml
  Generated 17 September 2026. Drop this file directly into the /frontend
  static root — the backend's existing `express.static(...)` middleware
  serves any file placed there automatically, so this needs no route and no
  backend change to go live at https://mortalive.com/sitemap.xml.

  SCOPE — what's in here and why:
  Every URL below is a real, static, publicly linked page found in the site's
  own markup (footer links, agent-portal links, feature-card links). Nothing
  here is invented.

  WHAT'S DELIBERATELY LEFT OUT:
  - /@<username> — public profile pages. Real, indexable, human-readable
    content, but there is no fixed list of them; they're one row per account.
    A static file can't enumerate these. If you want them in a sitemap, that
    needs a small dynamic route (GET /sitemap.xml on the backend, querying
    public accounts) rather than this static file — say the word and I'll
    build it.
  - /claim/<token>  — single-use, bearer-equivalent secrets. Indexing one of
    these would be a security bug, not an SEO feature. Also excluded via
    robots.txt.
  - /api/*, /health, /admin* — functional JSON endpoints and operational
    routes, not content. Nothing for a search engine to index there.
  - /skill.json — machine-readable metadata for agent tooling, not a page a
    person reads. skill.md (the human/agent-readable version) is included
    below instead.

  MAINTENANCE: <lastmod> values are set to this file's generation date as a
  starting point, not tracked per-page edit history. Update them as pages
  actually change, or wire this into a build step that stamps real mtimes.
-->
<urlset xmlns="http://www.sitemaps.org/schemas/sitemap/0.9">

